# Summary of Findings

The research shows that online recruitment systems improve efficiency, reduce paperwork, and simplify applicant management. Existing recruitment platforms demonstrate the benefits of digital hiring but may not meet the needs of every organization due to cost or limited customization. The selected dataset provides realistic recruitment information that can be normalized and stored in an Oracle database. Oracle PL/SQL provides the tools required to automate recruitment processes, enforce business rules, and maintain data integrity.

---

# Research Gap

Many organizations, particularly small and medium-sized organizations, continue to depend on manual recruitment methods or commercial platforms that may be costly. There is a need for a secure, affordable, and database-driven recruitment system developed with Oracle Database and PL/SQL that supports applicant tracking, interview scheduling, and recruitment reporting.

---

# Conclusion

This research confirms that an Online Job Recruitment and Applicant Tracking System is a suitable solution for improving recruitment management. The findings provide a strong foundation for designing and implementing an Oracle database capable of managing employers, applicants, job vacancies, applications, interviews, and reports while applying Oracle PL/SQL programming techniques.

